WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.760
Vibe coding is a conversational way to build and change software with an AI coding assistant.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.340
AI means artificial intelligence: a system that can generate text, code,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.120
and explanations from patterns it has learned.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:19.580
In this workflow, the developer describes an intended result, examines the assistant's output, gives feedback,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.080
and keeps refining until the project moves in the right direction.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:29.460
The experience can feel different from traditional coding because the developer may type fewer individual lines and

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.680
spend more time directing the work.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:38.060
You might describe a small web application, ask for a command-line utility, or request a refactor of duplicated code.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.440
The important activity shifts toward expressing intent, choosing boundaries, reading changes, testing behavior,

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.740
and deciding what belongs in the project.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.440
Productive vibe coding is not blind acceptance.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.220
Generated code can look plausible, use familiar names, and even run once while still violating a requirement.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.320
It might mishandle bad input, skip an authorization check, leak sensitive information,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.820
or create a design that will be difficult to maintain next month.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.000
A working demonstration is useful evidence, but it is not proof that the software is correct.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.900
The developer has to ask what was not exercised, who could be affected,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.520
and what assumptions are hiding in the implementation.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.420
This approach is especially helpful during exploration and prototyping.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.960
It can draft scaffolding, show how an unfamiliar application programming interface, or API, is usually called,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.420
produce a first version of tests, or suggest contained fixes for a failing case.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:37.480
Caution increases when the change touches authentication, payments, private data, infrastructure,

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.340
destructive operations, or a large codebase the developer does not yet understand.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.560
The central principle of this course is simple: the assistant can produce code, but the human owns the objective,

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.300
the boundaries, the evidence, and the final decision.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.960
Vibe coding is powerful when it shortens the distance between an idea and a testable experiment.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.660
It becomes risky when speed replaces understanding.
